warning[G008]: adds up a number that can't be added
 --> models/marts/monthly_completion.sql:3:5
  |
3 |     sum(completion_rate) as completion_rate
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ adds up ratios; a ratio can't be added
  |
 ::: models/intermediate/daily_completion.sql:4:5
  |
4 |     sum(case when status = 'complete' then 1 else 0 end) / count(*) as completion_rate
  |     --------------------------------------------------------------- a ratio is computed here
  |
  = note: adding ratios is not the ratio of the totals: 1/2 + 1/2 is 1, but 2/4 is 1/2
  = help: sum the numerator and the denominator separately per (date_trunc('month', order_date)), then divide
  = see: cardinal explain G008

warning[G008]: adds up a number that can't be added
 --> models/marts/region_aov.sql:4:5
  |
4 |     sum(a.avg_order_value) as summed_aov,
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ adds up averages; an average can't be added
  |
 ::: models/intermediate/customer_aov.sql:5:5
  |
5 |     avg(amount) as avg_order_value,
  |     ----------- an average is computed here
  |
  = note: a sum of averages grows with the number of groups, not with the values
  = help: sum the values and count the rows separately per (region, currency), then divide, or use avg() over the underlying rows
  = see: cardinal explain G008

warning[G008]: adds up a number that can't be added
 --> models/marts/region_aov.sql:5:5
  |
5 |     avg(a.avg_order_value) as mean_aov,
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ takes an average of averages; each counts the same however many rows it covers
  |
 ::: models/intermediate/customer_aov.sql:5:5
  |
5 |     avg(amount) as avg_order_value,
  |     ----------- an average per group
  |
  = note: an average of averages weights a group of one row like a group of a thousand
  = help: average the underlying rows per (region, currency), or weight each average by its row count: sum(avg_order_value * n) / sum(n)
  = see: cardinal explain G008

